# The root .gitignore ignores `audit/` (the legacy archive folder); with core.ignorecase on
# Windows that rule also swallowed app/Transform/Audit/. Re-include it explicitly.
!app/Transform/Audit/

# npm is the package manager here (`packageManager` in package.json pins it).
# A pnpm run in this directory during wave 4B wrote both of these and they were committed in
# 3f1d418; two lockfiles in one project is a CI trap, so a stray run can no longer be staged.
/pnpm-lock.yaml
/pnpm-workspace.yaml
/yarn.lock

# Database dumps: customer PII and password hashes. Never committed, never served.
/storage/app/backups

# ── The shared media tree. 631 MB on disk, and NONE of it belongs in git ───────────────────
#
# `MEDIA_ROOT` points here (config/media.php). It holds the product photography the legacy app
# and core both serve, plus a large cache of files no row references — kept deliberately, see
# CLEAN_CORE_STUDY §5.4.0, so nobody "tidies up" 56,000 files.
#
# It was NOT ignored until 2026-09-16, which on a PUBLIC repository meant one `git add -A` away
# from committing the whole image library. Found in the wave-4D reviewer's pass, before the first
# commit on the branch rather than after it.
/public/Uploads_Images

# Import run artifacts: supplier CSVs, fetched cover images, per-run reports. Working files that
# can name a supplier and carry their catalogue — they belong on the machine that ran the import.
/storage/import
